### How to use this
- Paste the code into any LaTeX editor (Overleaf, TeXstudio, etc.).
- Replace each “schematic” equation or sentence with your actual derived expressions.
- The `geometry` and `longtable` packages ensure margins and tables look professional.
- You can add sections for figures, references (`\bibliographystyle{unsrt}` + BibTeX), and appendices as needed.

This layout will produce a clean, journal-style document that unifies both your conceptual and derivation maps while keeping mathematics properly formatted and margin-compliant.
